    "percentage-change-calculator": { example: "Percentage change = (new value − original value) ÷ original value × 100. A move from 100 to 120 is a 20% increase; a move from 120 back to 100 is a 16.67% decrease because the baseline is now 120.", accuracy: "The original value is the denominator, so the calculation is undefined when the original value is zero. Negative baselines and values from different units or time periods need careful interpretation; the result is a mathematical comparison, not an explanation of why the value changed.", workflow: "Enter the starting value as the original and the later value as the new value. Keep both values in the same unit and compare like-for-like periods. Check whether the result is labelled as an increase or decrease before copying it.", mistakes: "Do not swap the original and new values. Do not confuse percentage change with percentage points or with the new value expressed as a percentage of the original. A reverse movement does not usually produce the same percentage magnitude." },
