    "salary-breakdown-calculator": { example: "A monthly gross salary of NPR 50,000 with a 10% illustrative deduction produces NPR 5,000 estimated deductions and NPR 45,000 take-home.", accuracy: "This is a simple deduction-rate estimate, not a Nepal statutory payroll or income-tax calculator. It does not model allowances, social security, provident fund or progressive tax bands.", workflow: "Enter gross monthly salary and an assumed deduction percentage. Compare the estimated monthly and annual take-home values with an actual payslip.", mistakes: "Do not use this simple deduction field as a substitute for the Nepal salary tax calculator or an employer's payroll statement." },
    "savings-goal-calculator": { example: "Monthly savings needed = (target − current savings) ÷ months remaining. For a target of 120,000 in your chosen currency, 30,000 already saved and 9 months remaining, set aside 10,000 per month. If you save NPR 2,500 each week instead, compare the total planned contributions with the target before the deadline.", accuracy: "This is a straight-line savings plan. It does not compound interest or include investment returns, inflation, fees, taxes, missed deposits or changing income. The monthly figure is a target, not a guaranteed outcome.", workflow: "Enter the final target amount, savings already set aside and the number of full months until the deadline. Check whether the target includes one-off costs, then divide the remaining amount into a realistic monthly plan. Recalculate after every deposit or deadline change.", mistakes: "Do not enter your current savings as an extra amount to add to the target. Use months remaining, not the total number of months since you started saving. Do not treat the estimate as an investment return or bank interest projection." },
